          "offset": 60,
          "skip": {
            "cpu": "the crash is driven by the player: the CPU rasteriser runs the junction at ~5 fps, and the title can then take more than one simulation step a frame (at least one a frame, sub_001B58E0), while the accelerator is held by the wall clock, so the car meets the traffic elsewhere; the shots before the GO (crash_intro, crash_caption) still match Metal"
          },
          "note": "bit-identical across Metal runs on toolkit fb3ca80; on 4a5572b (vblank sync to the display, present-early, two frames in flight) the impact comes 841-959 flips after the accelerator and the crash differs run to run (5 runs, load 6-7): open, see BO-54"
